  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "## Converting between Percentages and Fractions"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "A percentage is out of 100. We can re-write any percentage as a fraction by writing it over 100."
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 5: Convert 11% to a fraction.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "A percentage is the same as a fraction out of 100.\n\nWe can write 11% as 11⁄100",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 6: Convert 36% to a fraction. Give your answer in it simplest form.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "A percentage is the same as a fraction out of 100.\n\nWe can write 36% as 36⁄100\n\nWe have written 36% as a fraction, but it is not in its simplest form.  \nTo simplify we need to find a times table that 36 and 100 are both in.  \n36 and 100 are both in the 2 and the 4 times tables.  \n4 is the biggest so we will divide the denominator and the numerator by 4.\n\n36 = 4 × 9  \n100 = 4 × 25\n\n36% = 9⁄25\n\nWe could have also halved the top and bottom, and then halved again:\n\n36⁄100 = 18⁄50 = 9⁄25",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "To convert a fraction to a percentage we can change the denominator to 100."
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 7: Convert 7⁄20 to a percentage.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "To convert the fraction to a percentage we need to make the denominator 100.\n\nWe can make the denominator 100 by multiplying by 5.  \n20 × 5 = 100\n\nWe have to multiply the numerator by 5 too keep the fraction equivalent.  \n7 × 5 = 35\n\n7⁄20 = 35⁄100 = 35%",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
