  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "## Converting between Fractions and Decimals"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "To convert from a fraction to a decimal we can divide the numerator by the denominator."
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 8: Convert 3⁄8 to a decimal.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We can convert 3⁄8 to a decimal by calculating 3 ÷ 8.\n\nWe can use a calculator or short division to do the calculation.\n\n3 ÷ 8 = 0.375\n\n3⁄8 = 0.375\n\nIf we are using a calculator we can also use the SD button.",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 9 : Convert 7⁄12 to a decimal.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We need to calculate 7 ÷ 12\n\n7 ÷ 12 = $0.58\\dot3$\n\nThe dot above the 3 means that the 3 is recurring (it goes on forever), 0.5833333333333333333...\n\n7⁄12 = $0.58\\dot3$",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "mcq-set",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "78687f56-2b17-473d-ab9b-5c7055921835",
     "prompt": "Convert $\\frac{5}{8}$ to a decimal.",
